## Registry setup: prerequisite checks and Marketplace-aware help

Context: With Lakebase bound at install (option A), the remaining failure
points on a Marketplace install are permissions. These are the admin's scopes,
warehouse access, catalog privileges and schema ownership, plus the service
principal's Can Manage and its Lakebase access. The installer had no way to see
which one was missing, and several hints pointed at bootstrap scripts the
Marketplace bundle does not ship. The setup form gains a read-only "Check
prerequisites" panel that shows every check, as the admin and as the app's
service principal, each with a concrete fix. It runs automatically when setup
fails. Hints across the access-denied page, readiness checks and Initialize's
grant report now cover Marketplace installs. Verified live on a fresh install
(ontobricks-mp-test-014).

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/registry/RegistrySetupService.py
   New preflight(): read-only checks run as the caller. They cover the app's
   permissions (`apps` scope), the SP's Can Manage, SQL on the app's warehouse
   (`sql` scope), DESCRIBE CATALOG, and DESCRIBE SCHEMA EXTENDED (exists /
   owner / will be created). Each check is {name, label, status, detail, fix};
   the schema check is skipped when the catalog is unusable. Statement polling
   moved into a shared _execute(). Setup's privilege error now names the
   statement and points to Check prerequisites. The helpers are private
   static methods (class-first, src/.coding_rules.md §2).
2. src/back/objects/domain/settings/RegistrySettings.py
   New setup_check_result(); setup and check share _setup_service(), which
   requires the forwarded token and passes the caller's email (used in GRANT
   hints).
3. src/api/routers/internal/settings.py
   New admin-only POST /settings/registry/setup/check. The two setup routes
   share _run_registry_setup() (body validation, token and email).
4. src/front/templates/partials/registry/_registry_configuration.html
   "Check prerequisites" button, results grouped "As you" / "As the app's
   service principal" (aria-live), "Copy diagnostics", and a Troubleshooting
   section for the common cases.
5. src/front/static/config/js/settings-registry-configuration.js
   Runs the admin checks and the readiness checks in parallel, renders
   icon-and-label badges with a fix per check, collapses passing service
   principal checks, and copies the results as JSON (no tokens). The checks
   run automatically after a failed setup.
6. src/front/templates/access_denied.html
   The "bootstrap" reason now explains the Marketplace path (Set up the
   registry, or grant Can Manage in Apps → Permissions) before the repository
   `make bootstrap-perms`, and fixes the script path.
7. src/shared/fastapi/health.py
   A missing registry schema on a fresh install is a "not initialized yet"
   warning pointing to setup, not an error (shared _lakebase_probe_failure).
   registry.cfg and "Lakebase not bound" hints describe the Marketplace fix
   first. Script paths are corrected to scripts/bootstrap/lakebase-perms.sh.
   The baselined functions did not grow.
8. src/back/core/databricks/lakebase/grants.py
   Initialize's grant warnings explain when they are harmless: a missing MCP
   companion, CAN_USE on the Lakebase project, and the optional catalog-wide
   grant after setup.
9. docs/deployment.md, marketplace/LISTING.md, marketplace/README.md
   Document Check prerequisites and Copy diagnostics.
10. tests/units/registry/test_registry_setup_preflight.py (new),
    tests/units/registry/test_registry_setup.py,
    tests/units/front/test_settings_registry_setup_form.py,
    tests/units/core/test_health.py
    Cover the preflight checks (read-only, each failure's fix, skips), the
    check route (admin-only, caller's token and email), the UI contract, the
    access-denied text, and the fresh-install Lakebase warning.

