## Registry setup: clear error when no SQL warehouse is bound

Context: Simulating an install from scratch (ontobricks-mp-test-015, no
resources bound) showed that the admin's warehouse check reported "Can use on
SQL warehouse ``" with a blank ID, and setup failed with a raw API error.
Both now say to bind a `sql-warehouse` resource.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/registry/RegistrySetupService.py
   With no warehouse ID, preflight's warehouse check is an error with the
   binding fix (the dependent checks are skipped), and prepare() raises a
   ValidationError with the same fix before running any SQL.
2. tests/units/registry/test_registry_setup_preflight.py,
   tests/units/registry/test_registry_setup.py
   Cover both cases.

Modified files:
- src/back/objects/registry/RegistrySetupService.py
- tests/units/registry/test_registry_setup_preflight.py
- tests/units/registry/test_registry_setup.py

Tests: uv run --frozen pytest -q tests/units/registry tests/units/architecture tests/units/front → 3093 passed.
Live (ontobricks-mp-test-015, no resources): the warehouse check is an error
with the binding fix; the catalog and schema checks are skipped; the registry
stays unconfigured.
